      "description": "The album Drop Dead Fred by How Did This Get Made? is a live recording of a podcast episode originally released in 2019. It captures the comedic commentary and discussion of the 1991 cult film Drop Dead Fred by the podcast hosts, blending elements of stage performance and screen-related humor rather than traditional musical content. As such, it falls under the Non-Music, Stage & Screen genre and was self-released on the label Not On Label (How Did This Get Made? Self-released).\n\nThis release occupies a unique place in How Did This Get Made?'s discography as a live episode recording rather than a studio album, reflecting the podcast’s format of dissecting and humorously critiquing films. It showcases the group's dynamic interaction and comedic style in a live setting, featuring guest appearances such as Casey Wilson. While it does not have a commercial music chart presence or traditional critical reception, it is valued by fans of the podcast for its entertainment and insight into the film discussed.",
